.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt THREAD_CREATE 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm thread_create
.Nd create a thread in a process
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ft Handle
.Fn thread_create "Handle proc" "usize entry" "usize stack_top" "usize arg" "usize flags"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
system call creates a thread in
.Fa proc
at
.Fa entry
with the stack pointer
.Fa stack_top
and the first-argument register set to
.Fa arg .
All
.Fa flags
bits are reserved and must be zero.
.Pp
Admission is atomic with respect to process exit: the call either joins a live process or
fails; a process that has exited (through
.Xr exit 2 ,
its last
.Xr thread_exit 2 ,
or
.Xr proc_terminate 2 )
rejects the thread with
.Er ESRCH
and is never resurrected.  A failure after admission (a full handle table or run queue) rolls
the thread back.
.Pp
The returned handle carries
.Dv SIGNAL
and
.Dv DUP .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
On success
.Nm
returns the new thread handle; on failure it returns a negative error number.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EBADF
.Fa proc
is not a process handle.
.It Er EACCES
.Fa proc
lacks the
.Dv MAP
right, or the entry is not executable or the stack not writable in the target.
.It Er EFAULT
.Fa entry
or
.Fa stack_top
is outside the user range or unmapped.
.It Er EINVAL
Reserved flag bits are set, or the stack pointer is not 16-byte aligned.
.It Er ESRCH
.Fa proc
has no address space or is already terminal.
.It Er EAGAIN
The run queue is full.
.It Er EMFILE
The caller's handle table is full.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr exit 2 ,
.Xr proc_terminate 2 ,
.Xr thread_exit 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
